body:
**Critical bug**: The logic incorrectly handles unencoded block IDs, which will cause Azure API failures.

When `p.etag` starts with `'block-'`, it's the raw unencoded string (e.g., `'block-000001'`), but Azure requires base64-encoded block IDs. The current code uses this unencoded string directly, which will fail when calling `blockBlobClient.commitBlockList()`.

**Fix**:
```typescript
const blockList = sortedParts.map(p => {
  // If etag is already base64-encoded, use it
  if (p.etag.match(/^[A-Za-z0-9+/=]+$/) && !p.etag.startsWith('block-')) {
    return p.etag;
  }
  // Otherwise regenerate the properly encoded blockId
  return generateBlockId(p.partNumber);
});
```

The test at line 210 demonstrates this issue by passing `etag: 'block-000001'` (unencoded), which would be accepted but fail at Azure's API.
```suggestion

      const sortedParts = input.parts.sort((a, b) => a.partNumber - b.partNumber);
      const blockList = sortedParts.map(p => {
        // If etag is already base64-encoded, use it
        if (p.etag.match(/^[A-Za-z0-9+/=]+$/) && !p.etag.startsWith('block-')) {
          return p.etag;
        }
        // Otherwise regenerate the properly encoded blockId
        return generateBlockId(p.partNumber);
      });

```


